  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Three vertices of parallelogram \\(PQRS\\) are \\(P(-3,-2),\\) \\(Q(1,-5),\\) \\(R(9,1)\\) with \\(P\\) and \\(R\\) diagonally opposite. The sum of the coordinates of vertex \\(S\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(13\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "9"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1963-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(P+R=Q+S,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} S&=P+R-Q\\\\ &=(-3,-2)+(9,1)-(1,-5)\\\\ &=(5,4). \\end{aligned} \\] The coordinate sum is \\(5+4=9.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other",
        "Use the vector relation \\(P+R=Q+S\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
